Z||000003||Wolfhound||08-31-2001||01:44 PM||||I think there are several that will work from different GM engines but they have the timing marks in the wrong position. I had a spare 2.8 Balancer to replace it with. I also replaced the timing cover seal even though there was no sign the original was leaking.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DreXteR||08-31-2001||04:57 PM||||The deal is if CSB damper fits into the fieros engine then we ca use Fluidapr!!!  Another increase of power, maybe just a few but will be an increment.<P>About the time marks, summit sells some time marks sticker to place it in the damper. <P>DreX<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||08-31-2001||07:40 PM||||Make sure you get the right timing strip if you get one from summit or else where. those are calibrated to the circumfrence of the damper they go on. A small error can be a big problem.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DreXteR||09-01-2001||01:25 AM||||theogre - The time is not a big problem. You set the correct time with the original damper then change the fiero damper with the CSB fluidapr.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Of course if is a external one:   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DreX||||reg||1
